Let U ⊆ R'' be open and f: U -> R a function of class C². 
Suppose that a ∈ U is a critical point of f. 

	1) If the Hessian Hf(a) is positive definite, then f has a local minimum at a. 

	2) If the Hessian Hf(a) is negative definite, then f has a local maximum at a. 

	3) If det Hf(a) != 0 but Hf(a) is neither positive nor negative definite, then f has a saddle point at a. 
